    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d176">

                <pb facs="0312" n="222" sameAs="frus:frus1934v03/pg222"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.71 Manchuria/61</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Williamson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2613</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-07-19">July 19, 1934</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Reference is made to your despatch No. 3382
                    (L. N. No. 2274), dated June 6, 1934,<anchor n="51" xml:id="d176-f1"/> with
                    which there was forwarded Circular Letter No. 92, addressed to the Secretary of
                    State on June 4, 1934, by the Secretary-General of the League of Nations,<anchor
                        n="51" xml:id="d176-f2"/> and transmitting a circular of the Advisory
                    Committee on the Far Eastern situation relating to the question of postal
                    traffic in transit through Manchuria.</p>
                <p>There are enclosed the original and a copy of the reply of the American
                    Government to the communication above mentioned of the Secretary-General. It is
                    desired that you forward to the Secretary-General the original of this
                    Government’s reply. In so doing, please inform the Secretary-General that this
                    Government desires that the text of its reply be not made public or circularized
                    among the states <pb facs="0313" n="223" xml:id="pg223"/> members of the League
                    before the assent thereto of this Government has been given.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William
                            Phillips</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d176-a1.xml" xpointer="d176-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
